<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Singhasari</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Singhasari was a Javanese kingdom in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> in the thirteenth century. It expanded its influence into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, challenging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a>, and was overthrown in 1292. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit Empire</a> note that Majapahit arose from Singhasari's decline under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raden-wijaya">Raden Wijaya</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/singhasari.jpg" alt="Singhasari" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gunawan Kartapranata · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Singhasari_Kingdom_en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
